<!--
  Left bud — APP COPY, high-resolution trace.

  WHY THIS EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM ic_bud_left.xml
  The widget's bud icons were traced at a small scale and their outlines are
  visibly faceted: the widget draws them at ~30dp so the long shallow curves
  collapse to a few straight segments and nobody notices. The redesigned home
  screen shows the same buds at ~52dp and in the Find-my-earbuds screen at
  ~120dp, where those same segments read as jagged edges.

  A vector does NOT fix this on its own: the fault is in the PATH DATA (too few
  points along the curves), not in the rasteriser. Scaling the existing path up
  scales the facets up with it. So this file re-draws the same silhouette with
  the curves expressed as proper cubic segments, denser around the two places
  the old trace was worst — the outer shell of the stem and the ear-tip bowl.

  The silhouette is the same shape as ic_bud_left.xml, re-expressed with dense
  cubic segments so it stays smooth at 52dp in the app and 120dp in Find my
  earbuds. The stem's lower end is a ROUNDED cap (a semicircular arc), not the
  squared-off corner the first trace had — that corner was visible as a pointy
  tip at large sizes, which is what the user reported.

  Normalised the same way as the widget icons: ink centred on the viewport centre
  (24,24).
-->
